# Outputs, not sources. A stale capture silently compared against new code is
# exactly the trap this tool exists to remove, so they are never committed.
# ...but the capture SCRIPTS in there are sources by that same test, and every
# one of them was untracked -- including the pair.cfg LANE_START tells a lane to
# run. A cfg records which cvars a frame was taken under, which is the
# difference between a comparable pair and two unrelated pictures.
#
# This must exclude the CONTENTS (`captures/*`) and not the directory
# (`captures/`): git does not descend into an excluded directory, so with
# `captures/` the negation below silently does nothing.
captures/*
!captures/*.cfg
*.ridb
baseline.json

# Build products.
*.exe
*.dll
__pycache__/

# Savegames are GAME-DERIVED DATA and never go in the repo -- the same rule
# that keeps the retail install read-only. They are made once per map by hand
# (see warp_and_save.bat) and live here only so run_rothdiff can swap them
# into slot 0 without destroying each other.
saves/
